  "description": "Gate's service level objectives: availability, latency, usage freshness and event delivery, with burn rates. Definitions in docs/SLO.md; rules in observability/prometheus/rules/slo.yml.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "liveNow": false,
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Service level objectives",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Objectives (30-day rolling window; definitions in `docs/SLO.md`)\n\n| SLO | Good event | Objective | Budget |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Availability** | a `/v1` answer that is not a 5xx and not degraded (`X-Gate-Degraded`) | 99.9% | 0.1% (about 43 min of full outage) |\n| **Latency** | a `/v1` answer within 100 ms, measured at the server | 99% | 1% |\n| **Usage freshness** | a minute in which the aggregator's slowest shard is under 60 s behind | 99% | about 7 h 12 min |\n| **Event delivery** | a usage event that reaches Kinesis rather than being dropped | 99.9% | 0.1% |\n\nNot an SLO: **the limiters never over-issue.** That is an invariant with no budget, checked by `make correctness` and the TLA+ specs, never traded for availability.\n\nThese objectives are targets, not measured claims: no latency has been measured on real DynamoDB under load. Pages fire at 14.4x and 6x burn; tickets at 3x and 1x."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Objectives: 30 days",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
